>> title: Kafta
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: lamb, beef, lebanese, skewers, parsley, grill
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: kafta, kefta, kufta, kofta, kafta kabob, kafta kebab, kofte, köfte, lule kebab, minced meat skewers
>> pairs-with: pita-bread, sumac-onions, tahini-sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — ground lamb and beef on a skewer comes off cooked through and not pink, which is eight minutes over the fire
>> step.1: wring the onion dry
>> step.2: work the meat 3 min until it is tacky
>> step.3: chill the mix 30 min
>> step.4: press onto flat skewers
>> step.5: grill 8 min, turning once

Grate @yellow onion{1%medium}(150 g) and wring it out hard in a cloth.

Work @ground lamb{1%lb}(450 g; 20% fat), @ground beef{1/2%lb}(225 g), @&(~1)wrung onion{}, @flat-leaf parsley{1%cup}(chopped fine, packed), @ground allspice{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1%tsp} together with your hand ~beat{3%min}, always in one direction, until the mass turns tacky and holds a fingerprint.

Chill @&(~1)kafta mix{} covered ~chill{30%min}.

Press @&(~1)chilled mix{} onto @flat skewers{6} a handful at a time, squeezing it into a finger-thick sausage and pinching ridges every inch so the flame has something to catch.

Grill @&(~1)skewers{} over hot #charcoal grill{} coals ~grill{8%min}, turning once only, until the ridges char and the middle is just cooked through.
